//! **Generated by `vendor/research/mtproto/gen_schema.py` from `api.tl`. Do not
//! edit.** Regenerate when the layer changes; see `rpc::LAYER`.
//!
//! # Why this exists
//!
//! Reading a chat list means parsing `messages.Dialogs`, which reaches **495
//! constructors**. TL is not self-describing, so a field cannot be skipped without
//! knowing its type — a parser that wants six fields of `message` still has to walk
//! the forty in front of them, and several of those are nested constructor families
//! of their own.
//!
//! Hand-writing that is most of a megabyte of source. Hand-writing *part* of it is
//! worse: a parser that guesses at a field it does not know is off by however many
//! bytes that field was, and every value after it is garbage that still parses.
//!
//! So the walker knows the shapes and nothing else. It reads a boxed value by
//! reading its constructor id and looking it up here, which means a field of an
//! unexpected type is an unknown constructor rather than a silent misparse.

